If a patient takes an opioid during at least 1 year then it is possible that a taper continues during some months and it is possible that a taper continues during some years.
If a patient takes an opioid during at least 1 year then it is possible that a taper-duration depends on an opioid-dosage.
If a patient receives a long-term-opioid-therapy then it is possible that a taper continues during some months and it is possible that a taper continues during some years.
If a patient receives a long-term-opioid-therapy then it is possible that a taper-duration depends on an opioid-dosage.
If a patient receives a long-term-opioid-therapy and has a taper and has a patient-goal then every clinician should individualize the taper with the patient-goal.
If a patient receives a long-term-opioid-therapy and has a taper and has a patient-concern then every clinician should individualize the taper with the patient-concern.
